Present timing: per presented frame, when its command buffers were submitted, when Present
returned and when the GPU finished it (a helper thread waits on an OnSubmittedWorkDone future per
frame; with a variable refresh rate display that is about when the frame is shown). Also
aurora_wait_frame_done, so the host can keep the GPU at most one frame behind. LM uses it to pace
interpolated presentation and to log display times (src/recomp/pacing.cpp, docs/INTERPOLATION.md).
Off until aurora_present_timing_enable(true).

